WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.066 --> 00:00:01.468
- I never talked about this. For three—

00:00:01.468 --> 00:00:07.240
Even in Toronto.
My dad got sick Christmas 2018.

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:11.011
My last year in Toronto,
my dad got sick. Went to the hospital.

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:13.646
I flew home
a couple days before Christmas,

00:00:14.981 --> 00:00:18.051
sat with my dad, and he was in the hospital

00:00:18.651 --> 00:00:21.755
for the next—in and out of the hospital
the next three years after that.

00:00:21.755 --> 00:00:24.290
So for three years,

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:28.028
I flew from Boston to L.A.,
L.A. to Toronto

00:00:28.461 --> 00:00:32.499
by myself, played in the game.
Did the same thing in San Antonio. And nobody

00:00:32.499 --> 00:00:34.968
never knew. It was times that I flew
in the day of the game and played.

00:00:35.969 --> 00:00:39.839
From seeing my dad.
- So, leave L.A.,

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:43.810
fly in game day and play
that night.
- That night.

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:46.880
I did it so many times, countless times.
I never talked about it.

00:00:47.147 --> 00:00:48.214
Never talked about it.

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:50.283
- I mean, how difficult was that

00:00:50.283 --> 00:00:53.119
when you were making these trips
and then having to go to work?

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:55.722
- It was, it was, it was the most—

00:00:55.722 --> 00:01:00.060
It was probably the hardest thing
in my life to do because you know, you,

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:04.898
you, you have so much idle
time of sitting on a plane by yourself,

00:01:06.266 --> 00:01:08.601
dealing with the emotional, like,

00:01:09.903 --> 00:01:14.040
like, trauma of seeing your dad,
seeing a person that—only person in life

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:17.110
I ever feared—you know, down and out,

00:01:18.278 --> 00:01:20.880
to having to go play
in front of 20,000 people.

00:01:21.381 --> 00:01:24.350
You know, it was like
the emotional roller coaster

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:27.087
that I dealt with for,
you know, three years was,

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:31.091
was one of the toughest things ever
because, one, I never wanted to be

00:01:31.091 --> 00:01:35.862
a distraction to my teammates,
to the game and nothing.

00:01:35.862 --> 00:01:37.764
So I dealt with everything

00:01:37.764 --> 00:01:39.933
I dealt with personally,
and I didn't want to be loud about it.

00:01:39.933 --> 00:01:43.403
I didn't want nobody necessarily
feel sorry for me and everything,

00:01:43.403 --> 00:01:46.973
but I also wanted to be there
for my teammates and my family.

00:01:47.006 --> 00:01:50.844
You know what I mean? So to carry
those emotions consistently,

00:01:51.411 --> 00:01:54.481
you know, behind the scenes
and nobody knew, you know, it was, it was,

00:01:54.981 --> 00:01:56.416
it was tough. It was tough.

00:01:56.416 --> 00:02:00.854
Like, even, even when I lost my dad,
I was in a hotel in Charlotte.

00:02:01.121 --> 00:02:04.424
Just finished playing a game. Fly home.

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:08.495
You know, home a couple of days.
And I flew back with the team to play in

00:02:08.495 --> 00:02:12.298
a game. Fly back home. Go to his funeral.
Leave shootaround. Go play in a—

00:02:12.565 --> 00:02:15.401
You know, it was like
all those emotions to where–

00:02:16.136 --> 00:02:18.171
And then what really made it hard,

00:02:18.171 --> 00:02:21.975
you know, like I said, I'm sitting
on a plane by myself for hours, like,

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:26.012
you know, with this on your mind
trying to figure out how,

00:02:26.045 --> 00:02:29.649
how are you going to balance yourself
out to be able to play tonight?

00:02:29.883 --> 00:02:33.720
You know? But I needed to play.
Like I said, my teammates, guys

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:35.922
I played with knew
what I was going through,

00:02:35.922 --> 00:02:39.292
and they was always there for me,
and they made it easy for me, and that's why

00:02:39.292 --> 00:02:43.263
I always felt like I had to be there
for them as well to compete.
- Yeah.

00:02:44.063 --> 00:02:45.965
- So, yeah, that was for three years.

